  "articleBody": "Ever painted a wall after a storm repair, only to find it looks patchy or uneven? It's a common frustration, and usually, it boils down to a few key mistakes. One of the biggest culprits is painting over damp drywall. If the underlying material isn't completely dry, the paint won't adhere correctly, leading to an uneven finish and potential future problems. Another frequent error is skipping the primer. Primer creates a consistent surface for the paint to grip, and without it, your paint can soak into different materials at varying rates, causing patchiness. Failing to properly feather or blend patched areas with joint compound before painting is also a major no-no; any bumps or lines will show right through the new paint. Lastly, not matching the paint's sheen or finish type can make repairs super visible. Even if the color is spot on, a different sheen will create a noticeable contrast. If your finish work isn't looking quite right, or if you’re dealing with recurring stains, it's a good sign that professional help, like that offered by HH Remodeling LLC, might be necessary to stabilize the repair and achieve a smooth, consistent look.",
